; The mirror of tuck-under.bel: the same pocket tuck, named from below. .q sits
; on the base layer, so `over .q` lands the block immediately above the base —
; between the two layers, the same stack `under` the top layer's remainder
; produces. A plain fold of the same corner would put it on top of everything
; and its crease would read mountain; here the corner ends up under the layer
; it hinges to, and the crease reads valley.

paper square

fold map .a onto .d                     ; bottom half up onto the top half
.m = free on --bc from .b at 1/2        ; (1, 1/2): on the crease, both layers
.n = free on --ab from .b at 1/2        ; (1/2, 0) on the paper, table (1/2, 1)
.q = free on --cd from .d at 1/4        ; (1/4, 1) on the paper: the base layer
fold --t = through .m .n moving .b over .q

; assert steps = 2
; assert faces = 3
; assert --t is valley
